    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "22e6c238_144f5c8c",
        "filename": "graphics/mapper/4.0/types.hal",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 125,
      "author": {
        "id": 1073546
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-30T22:33:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Previously for any buffer with a variable bytesPerStride, we had gralloc return a -1. \n\nWhat is the advantage of return in a \u003e\u003d0 value for a compressed buffer? Is there any use case for it?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 125,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 125,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "fd57a8232f51b61dc62ec447eb8302d79d7b8980",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bdd15b25_820aa812",
        "filename": "graphics/mapper/4.0/types.hal",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 125,
      "author": {
        "id": 1029699
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-04T17:55:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "hmm... negative stride means pixels are bottom up. If we allow negative stride in plane descriptor (as use int32 instead of uint32), I don\u0027t think it is good practice to repurpose -1 as an indication that stride is not applicable. We could use 0 instead. \nwe use uint32 here because we don\u0027t want negative stride to be used.",
      "parentUuid": "22e6c238_144f5c8c",
